    {
      "id": "headerPadding",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "header padding",
      "form": {
        "of": "opaque"
      },
      "about": [
        "RFC 9293 §3.1: 'The content of the header beyond the End of Option List Option MUST be header",
        "padding of zeros', and Data Offset counts 32-bit words, so the options have to reach a word",
        "boundary.",
        "",
        "A field that computes how wide it needs to be, rather than something the walk does quietly. Without",
        "it a six-octet option run gives a twenty-six octet header and a Data Offset of six — off by half a",
        "word, and wrong in a way every field after it inherits."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.padding",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "the zeros that reach a word boundary",
      "runs": "\"00\" |> unhex() |> repeat((4 - (sets.options.extent % 4)) % 4)",
      "about": [
        "The padding's VALUE, not its width. A field that computed how wide it was while its value said",
        "something else would have two answers to what it lays down, and the engine refuses the second",
        "— which is right: an extent is a fact about a value, and giving it one of its own means the",
        "two can disagree.",
        "",
        "RFC 9293 §3.1: 'The content of the header beyond the End of Option List Option MUST be header",
        "padding of zeros', and Data Offset counts 32-bit words, so the options run has to reach one."
      ]
    },
